From: Linux Fieldwork <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] executor: clean stubs from the finalized OCI mount list

MountStubsCleaner currently sees only BuildKit's explicit execution mounts.
Default OCI mounts are added later by GenerateSpec, and rootless conversion
then removes the unsupported /sys mounts. As a result, runc can create an
empty /sys mountpoint in a rootful scratch snapshot while the matching
rootless execution creates no such directory.

Register cleanup after the OCI spec is finalized and rootless-adjusted. Feed
it the actual spec mount destinations, remove deeper empty stubs before their
parents, and retain the existing rule that paths already present before
execution are never removed.

This keeps ownership mode-correct: rootful owns the /sys stub because its
final spec mounts sysfs there; rootless does not own /sys because ToRootless
removed that mount.
---
 executor/containerdexecutor/executor.go      |  2 ++
 executor/containerdexecutor/executor_unix.go |  1 -
 executor/runcexecutor/executor.go             |  3 ++-
 executor/stubs.go                             | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

